<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>EU drops sanctions for Russian oligarchs Usmanov and Fridman</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e34094cf1a2e1f54411c2d6a7f586228dc248891c03f81266e90e814e7c07ce7</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T19:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-drops-sanctions-for-russian-oligarchs-usmanov-and-fridman/a-79381048--fa0b2b1f5563.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-drops-sanctions-for-russian-oligarchs-usmanov-and-fridman/a-79381048?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France and Luxembourg were behind the sanctions exemptions for Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman, a move that Kyiv labeled "shameful and unjustifiable."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Amateur archeologist unearths Germany's largest trove of Roman coins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6afecdcbc3a379491c99431a87c408b4ee05e15a2ec9ba24395c3c2ea8571274</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T17:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amateur-archeologist-unearths-germany-s-largest-trove-of-roman-coins/a-79379127--cd97ff72e024.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amateur-archeologist-unearths-germany-s-largest-trove-of-roman-coins/a-79379127?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">What began as a routine search in a field near Wesseling led to the discovery of nearly 1,000 Roman silver coins, one of the most significant archaeological finds in Germany in recent years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Military aircraft crashes near US air base in Spangdahlem, Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e166ddaeb1ceb063fdd5d12a28bc0883321ac75a93fed5da8e8d360a2160e102</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/military-aircraft-crashes-near-us-air-base-in-spangdahlem-germany/a-79376025--82e638c408d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/military-aircraft-crashes-near-us-air-base-in-spangdahlem-germany/a-79376025?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The F-16 pilot was able to safely eject from the plane and was taken to receive medical care. The incident occurred near Spangdahlem Air Base in the German state of Rhineland-Palatinate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US-China AI race: Does Trump want to regulate AI by forming a new task force and a special envoy for artificial intelligence in the US?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14e5a537218cc2ffd76fe83f7aa485929ec7e50127535f0e06413a24f5646cd9</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-china-ai-race-does-trump-want-to-regulate-ai-by-forming-a-new-task-force-and-a-special-envoy-for-/a-79372591--6f057766415d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-china-ai-race-does-trump-want-to-regulate-ai-by-forming-a-new-task-force-and-a-special-envoy-for-artificial-intelligence-in-the-us/a-79372591?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Do Trump's task force and a special envoy for artificial intelligence in the US indicate a move toward regulating this disputed technology, particularly vis-a-vis China?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Young Berliners vote overwhelmingly for socialist Left  Party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce7d6c0d5476cc03bfcd65e54f7bcf728bcf1f1d24285ba1eedbee32785188e8</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/young-berliners-vote-overwhelmingly-for-socialist-left-party/a-79375167--9c7d9060df7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/young-berliners-vote-overwhelmingly-for-socialist-left-party/a-79375167?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin's young voters overwhelmingly supported the victorious socialist Left Party. Are the young more radical? Or are the election results just a reflection of current German politics?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Living in the shadow of LA's hidden oil wells</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b87d0a56546acf2d8c949c3b7b2fb1b6104c28f77ac70f22006ab9dfc1182a03</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T13:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/living-in-the-shadow-of-la-s-hidden-oil-wells/a-79237420--13c7836e2425.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/living-in-the-shadow-of-la-s-hidden-oil-wells/a-79237420?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Many lifelong residents of Los Angeles have health impacts from growing up close to oil extraction. Now, the city is trying to close down the worst offenders, but it's an enormous task.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>After floods, Nepal minister demands 'climate justice'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2e5ab692afc0ccd35714e27033b848d901e58acb02def037e87344e4edc4cd3</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-floods-nepal-minister-demands-climate-justice/a-79372239--033ba1d032f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-floods-nepal-minister-demands-climate-justice/a-79372239?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With Nepal still reeling from the devastating floods in August, Kathmandu is calling for climate justice and seeking compensation from the UN-backed Loss and Damage Fund, Environment Minister Geeta Chaudhary told DW.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Could we see MMA at the Olympics?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d33c9e1cb7261c7f586006a4afde918ff97dc51aa32834712fd728ebc889bfc</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-we-see-mma-at-the-olympics/a-79369605--f76e8af14c92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-we-see-mma-at-the-olympics/a-79369605?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mixed martial arts has made its debut at the Asian Games this week. It takes the sport closer to the Olympics but there are doubts about the next step, and the influence of the popular and lucrative UFC.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war spreads through region as Trump seeks way out</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b26290406f5e56fe95434825ed641072b7935be20382f3c2dfd964a0815faedb</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T11:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-spreads-through-region-as-trump-seeks-way-out/a-79370506--a1fa6d225e80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-spreads-through-region-as-trump-seeks-way-out/a-79370506?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Washington, Tehran and the Gulf states continue to pursue different objectives while searching for a way to end the Iran war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Several pupils injured in shooting outside school</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc01139b8fc4fa21e3f385dff3f1637798c7a7ec95c631326ea5ced21a92da1f</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-several-pupils-injured-in-shooting-outside-school/a-79368728--cc52dff21bd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-several-pupils-injured-in-shooting-outside-school/a-79368728?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The shooter, a pupil, allegedly took a rifle and shot indiscriminately at his schoolmates in front of their high school. Turkey was shocked by two back-to-back school shootings earlier this year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia, Ukraine trade deadly strikes as Zelenskyy attends UNGA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:621687360b1953f0c0398adf5c640e2a2b930f7c9619c6ed2e160d2f92c07c71</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-ukraine-trade-deadly-strikes-as-zelenskyy-attends-unga/a-79366022--933d7c07ec6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-ukraine-trade-deadly-strikes-as-zelenskyy-attends-unga/a-79366022?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Russian army targeted economic infrastructure in Ukraine, while Ukraine struck an oil refinery. This comes ahead of the UN General Assembly, where President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is due to meet Trump on the sidelines.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Male infertility is 'grossly underreported'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be098fe8fb7276d6ce76456311ff41a0825505521d38c2389d6ed9053058caf9</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722--14a06576edd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's not all on women anymore — doctors do test men for sperm count and motility. But still too few men get checked, possibly due to a misconception that a healthy sex life means healthy sperm. Spoiler: It doesn't.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>UN General Assembly opens with Trump, Lula, others in NYC</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddc824197aeee97ed158a74cf05af89e2ae9d742694f3be3eb6a1025b20a58b8</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T08:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-general-assembly-opens-with-trump-lula-others-in-nyc/live-79366211--22b571c749d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-general-assembly-opens-with-trump-lula-others-in-nyc/live-79366211?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump hailed his own record and hinted at a chance for peace in Iran and Ukraine. Turkey's president called for more pressure on Israel. UN leaders called for more global interdependence. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Swan Song': New book by Princess Diana's brother drops</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd22dc75bc36534c7444afc1085fb25b6461bffc432e6cd78edb4adafd034248</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/swan-song-new-book-by-princess-diana-s-brother-drops/a-79365835--93fce9a8a45c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/swan-song-new-book-by-princess-diana-s-brother-drops/a-79365835?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A memoir penned by Charles Spencer on his older sister's life has been released, opening old royal wounds nearly three decades after Princess Diana's death.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Will Germany have enough gas this winter amid energy supply crunch?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5176e1b2688923cb811f190de6b330558e02e2740faf7e6cc6862f906530f5d</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-germany-have-enough-gas-this-winter-amid-energy-supply-crunch/a-79360317--cfd94c55c93d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-germany-have-enough-gas-this-winter-amid-energy-supply-crunch/a-79360317?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's gas storage sites are far less full than in recent years. Officials say supplies are secure, but analysts warn that a cold winter or import disruptions could push prices higher. So how secure is the supply?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: VW to step up cost-cutting program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fb79fbccda37aa75cd7ad0f1add3ef541fa0c058a449cff96d913e2ae687fd5</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T07:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-vw-to-step-up-cost-cutting-program/live-79365190--a755a3e03dbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-vw-to-step-up-cost-cutting-program/live-79365190?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Volkswagen's chief says the carmaker will accelerate its streamlining measures as workers protest. The Israeli ambassador says the Left Party win in Berlin polls poses a risk to the city's Jewish community. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How will Germany's Merz respond after crushing state election results and losses to the far right?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ecc004d69f0c30832a46b9f04161d15f56d83f9d6df8d4e023fbd4088115667</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-will-germany-s-merz-respond-after-crushing-state-election-results-and-losses-to-the-far-right/a-79365325--120a3b5033f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-will-germany-s-merz-respond-after-crushing-state-election-results-and-losses-to-the-far-right/a-79365325?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD and the socialist Left Party gained ground in recent state elections, while the centrist parties lost support. The biggest loser is Chancellor Friedrich Merz.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Princess Diana's brother makes explosive claims about royals in new memoir</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d395ee42fd453667784e292fd314a7ed21d45c7426977f9f6cfadf6bb3c93358</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/princess-diana-s-brother-makes-explosive-claims-about-royals-in-new-memoir/a-79309465--3d900d102240.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/princess-diana-s-brother-makes-explosive-claims-about-royals-in-new-memoir/a-79309465?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Here are some of the key revelations from Charles Earl Spencer's highly anticipated memoir "Swan Song: Diana, My Sister." It has already provoked Buckingham Palace to react.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Police investigate alleged gang-rape in Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fffc834843fdd892a490db87c6bf8aba5033cef42a7bf22ebe5382e4c2672084</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T06:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-police-investigate-alleged-gang-rape-in-delhi/live-79365177--41caa0443681.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-police-investigate-alleged-gang-rape-in-delhi/live-79365177?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While India is fuming over a viral video of two minors being harassed in Bihar, a case of an alleged gang-rape of a minor has emerged in a posh Delhi neighborhood. Meanwhile, India's foreign minister is at the UNGA.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>G7 demands Houthis 'immediately' cease Saudi strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5689f1adc891ff1755ee9679166333e546f1d9cbdf7c53d612cc3d85faceea09</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T04:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/g7-demands-houthis-immediately-cease-saudi-strikes/a-79364964--b1476907806f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/g7-demands-houthis-immediately-cease-saudi-strikes/a-79364964?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The G7 nations have accused Yemen's Houthi rebels of targeting civilian shipping near Saudi Arabia. UK PM Andy Burnham said he will offer "time-limited" and "defensive" military support to repel the attacks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Trial starts of ex-Transport Minister Scheuer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06321eddd004263cdb2bc3b5ab3ab03cbabf786380ebec8e877cdf03df1d3c86</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-trial-starts-of-ex-transport-minister-scheuer/live-79351160--5052118e7b45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-trial-starts-of-ex-transport-minister-scheuer/live-79351160?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Transport Minister Andreas Scheuer is being tried for perjury related to a failed car toll scheme. And cherry farmers have brought in a bumper harvest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's car crisis: Can the 35-hour workweek survive?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d38c45a96542605fac2ee0cd8b7e8f381ef45c49d07c8ef98c6621ff24ff8ad2</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488--cb2e3220b33e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German carmakers want employees to work 40 hours instead of the current 35 without extra pay, arguing it would improve competitiveness. Unions strongly oppose the proposal and view it as an attack on workers' rights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>German state elections deal a blow to Chancellor Friedrich Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75713001aa21a3825f6c42e644aeb193cb2c9a292d54f70b363503024e910f77</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T21:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585--45dd8fc79779.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elections in Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania have dealt the CDU a historic defeat while the AfD saw a massive gain. The pressure on Germany's unpopular chancellor is mounting.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>AfD makes gains in state elections but has no government options</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:276d45c0853b7cca331a786b7470a8e73c4433eb480c0bba063e612b4b09c244</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T19:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-makes-gains-in-state-elections-but-has-no-government-options/a-79348308--1a6e760f93a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-makes-gains-in-state-elections-but-has-no-government-options/a-79348308?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite making significant gains in both Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, the far-right AfD remains without options to form a state government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces energy tax losses as EV sales rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9755d39710fc28bf53e48f48d6e8b707f1d8c1b337d052ef9cd95046356342d7</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422--82b05ee44dbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The rapid shift to electric vehicles in Germany is cutting fuel tax revenue for the government. As EV sales surge, policymakers face growing pressure to find new ways to fund roads and transportation infrastructure.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>In cosmopolitan Berlin, elections still closed to foreigners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dccb9f9734f264d88d10a936efa5cfe4d374a58234188bc434affaceb5c4bb44</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579--2c7a3b66c58f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter of Berlin residents will have no say in the German capital's city-state election because they lack citizenship. That's the highest proportion of residents excluded from the election yet, and many are unhappy.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Doctors offer Oktoberfest flu jabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09bc007032f013c2b8b0d73482aa39e64b27eedb4c8fdcd3b47c13ba0439cfef</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548--b4ec07a0d158.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest 2026 is underway but it's not just beer on offer in Munich this year; revelers can also get themselves a flu jab before heading to the tents. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is it possible to replace the chancellor?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d4f5a38c2600fd52e687a522ac2e8bc5549b54a7efbf7393c6e933a556ee32c</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T05:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623--5363f1668974.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz's record-low approval ratings have emboldened his opponents. There are three ways to remove a chancellor from office in Germany.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Summer of 2026 broke records in Europe, and caused deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fa1d1f82c17ca9e3ac7319095dc9884f0a265bdf3cf68cef5d9cde6284ce0a1</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T19:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/summer-of-2026-broke-records-in-europe-and-caused-deaths/a-79339630--5efe97f5474b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/summer-of-2026-broke-records-in-europe-and-caused-deaths/a-79339630?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The summer of 2026 was not only the hottest on record in Europe, it also saw a record number of people die. More than 16,000 are thought to have died because of the heat in Germany alone.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>German-Russian relations at freezing point</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4746ce502169e98b41555bbcb84c066c4c42ce4f5b180558606aa6869891a2e</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-russian-relations-at-freezing-point/a-79330741--08a579f047c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-russian-relations-at-freezing-point/a-79330741?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine destroyed the once-close relationship between Moscow and Berlin. Yet the far-right AfD is calling for a normalization of relations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine steps up measures to protect railways</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0fe29c7401def52cdf3e5e12aa99e26168b1c4bea09a5751f037389ef5855d0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-steps-up-measures-to-protect-railways/a-79339087--356ca60a409d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-steps-up-measures-to-protect-railways/a-79339087?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia increases its attacks on Ukraine's rail infrastructure, the Ukrainian government has called for help to replace destroyed locomotives and is making plans to keep passengers safe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania: Will economy shape the vote?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d55521758e7804a0a28a8a55e4d72d8b86a1b12e8af250ffcdb0de63217d9807</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-will-economy-shape-the-vote/a-79298904--432385452f89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-will-economy-shape-the-vote/a-79298904?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Voters in the eastern state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania head to the polls on Sunday, with the Social Democrats and far-right AfD neck and neck. Here's a look at key economic issues that could influence the election.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c8ac6e21a14196946084ac027ac1ab556095261f5e2cb3d72402cef5a61a7ec</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This year, AI will be used to manage overcrowded situations. Find all the numbers surrounding the fest — including the price of water!</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Rebels, workers, radicals: The making of 'Red Berlin'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbceeff11d2703d69c2b6bbc4079877a81e021f23a20a76d52bd2457cbcefbed</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410--afcfe0d2ce3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bloody May, student sit-ins and the squatter movement: Berlin has long been a hotbed for working-class organizing and radical left-wing politics.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania: SPD seeks to fend off AfD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6569aa0391b57be21125f74558c0dd23124f968dc3a04df050eae348a6b4cb95</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-spd-seeks-to-fend-off-afd/a-79330234--336ea67c69c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-spd-seeks-to-fend-off-afd/a-79330234?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For nearly three decades, the Social Democrats have governed Germany's northeastern state. If they can fend off the AfD, the result may boost the fortunes of the German government's junior coalition partner.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ever more Israelis moving to and investing in Cyprus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:335ee95ab3c4c8adfcfc8995ec4fa347912c1e76e808b823c89f5b459203c9c0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240--f9d83a8ed500.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past three years, more and more Israelis have been purchasing property and investing in Cyprus, with many moving to the island permanently. How has this changed the Cypriot economy and how are locals responding?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football in Germany booming, but still much to do</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5ea10f43316743f98511babd761d8e3d4895445a968d33513bb342b953aa6ac</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T04:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687--313365dcb46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women's football is growing rapidly, particularly in Germany. Nevertheless, equal pay and investment remain major talking points.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz attacks spill oil into Persian Gulf</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19d6140c91c3e224d977291a5cd5b7d18cce82acae8149d025a3015b3c06cead</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092--09836173253c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As war disrupts one of the world's busiest shipping lanes, satellite images reveal that oil is spreading toward protected coral reefs and mangrove forests.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Airport malaria in Germany remains infrequent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7277ff7ef578fb9e8f92bebd9f2e8122002de4d696d3b67207701cfde57dee53</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920--b6e9f1b4961f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An outbreak of malaria at Frankfurt Airport this summer has raised alarm. Experts believe parasites probably arrived in a passenger's luggage. But with the onset of fall, the risks of contracting the disease are low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact Check: False video alleges Berlin votes destroyed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c625a6335b0b8fe18254391591ead8a0f6484d551f447cc058455e6d651f1f71</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-false-video-alleges-berlin-votes-destroyed/a-79333344--411939a21d7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-false-video-alleges-berlin-votes-destroyed/a-79333344?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A video claiming to show AfD postal ballots being destroyed has gone viral ahead of Berlin's September 20 election. DW Fact Check examines the footage, the accounts sharing it and how widely it is really being viewed.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German police probe arson attack on Wuppertal synagogue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:216c5bd7f9a6a3e576c8d184cc5149b5132e847ffdbd2495000804bfff7f6360</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-arson-attack-on-wuppertal-synagogue/a-79331270--dce70b32746f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-arson-attack-on-wuppertal-synagogue/a-79331270?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man detained shortly after allegedly trying to set fire to Wuppertal's synagogue made antisemitic comments to the arresting officers, prosecutors say. The 37-year-old Afghan citizen also had knives in his apartment.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada and EU: A look at the bloc's special relationships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae49cbedb8c408cf53481a2ea757820526de3288879864f8a0f66bd32f8e1381</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-and-eu-a-look-at-the-bloc-s-special-relationships/a-79328797--41616c65f5bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-and-eu-a-look-at-the-bloc-s-special-relationships/a-79328797?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Though Canada may be some distance from Europe geographically, closer political ties are in the cards. With talk of an associate membership, DW takes a look at other arrangements the EU has with particular countries.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Dual citizenship means Germany now in competition for talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0537129a1a04fb2bfbc4497964f14a0827b2bf0ad86f39b773c4aed178eff4b5</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797--d43696518a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Coach Jürgen Klopp has named several players to his first Germany squad who are eligible to play for other countries. Some still aren't committed to playing for thje national team long-term.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Beethoven and Andy Warhol: Rebel icons on show in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d0e11fd1940a0da2ce3a14a8920938fb6a4e4ac4696d383360bc2eee764e6e7</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944--59ad6d6535a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new exhibition "Beethoven by Warhol" at the Beethoven House in Bonn presents the pop artist's late masterpiece: a picture of Ludwig van Beethoven. The exhibition shares the story of the work with the public.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>'No compromises': Far-right AfD has few potential partners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3cd7d67d449ddf3c4f29ea5a0f5505b4dd6413fe220980d43cc6bc1a8b8d34b</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-compromises-far-right-afd-has-few-potential-partners/a-79326208--c5bd1a26f736.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-compromises-far-right-afd-has-few-potential-partners/a-79326208?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD party is riding high after its latest electoral triumph in Saxony-Anhalt. But one question remains: Does it actually want to govern?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>VAR's mission creep a problem for football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78e0298b1f33e7ad2dbb604d79367a5bb28c2e082cde2b3da1e3bf3808b648f8</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642--644b469bed29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a decade of use, questions around VAR in football are louder than ever. Has the technology strayed too far from its remit?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Organized crime and drug-related deaths rise Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38b975413ff131f5a13f21af2b9462ebb480336be95a732c922f8fb7497ae1a9</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/organized-crime-and-drug-related-deaths-rise-germany/a-79315774--74932d6d2d5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/organized-crime-and-drug-related-deaths-rise-germany/a-79315774?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the annual report on organized crime, German police say cocaine is a danger for the state and society and cases of money laundering have increased.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Russian birth tourism to Brazil increases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0ca1b22cdd993d2c89e0372dd38c5143740a45aa720ba51c3ae940355a561ff</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T19:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304--01a0fcbb92e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine and stricter regulations in Argentina, more and more Russians are choosing to travel to Brazil to give birth to children, who will obtain Brazilian nationality.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A war-fatigued and anxious Russia picks a new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03cfbe1b05944acd539d9484eed3637c7e797de63853e23bf42b605f5f0e82b5</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440--1588122e0cc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.co