ssia's recent drone attacks on targets close to the Ukraine-Poland border, Warsaw has doubled down on its support for Kyiv and pledged a "nonprovocative but serious response" to Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Global Gender Gap Report: Women's hard-won gains 'fragile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13ad7ce0d12fc9a8d48e73ba641911b1c71b25914830df0b832e893b03aad2b7</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086--9ed95bd98a77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two decades of progress toward gender parity is at risk as women's political representation declines, according to a new World Economic Forum report. At the current pace, the remaining gap could take 120 years to close.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo ex-president Thaci sentenced to 25 years for war crimes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:870365efa28c4198ac865b2d0033b6600dfd3fda9f3fc5470c30e9cbd7915718</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344--737389b3e2ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Hague tribunal ruled that Hashim Thaci, a former leader of the Kosovo Liberation Army (KLA), is responsible for war crimes carried out during the war of independence with Serbia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German drama 'Blindspot Berlin' revisits 2016 Christmas market attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6831b5623e4804d424fd45349a3831ff1fa2ff12c27663b6c24b07924229e920</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162--11e3e3b69ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the terrorist attack on a Berlin Christmas market, a new German miniseries looks into the institutional failures that allowed the deadly truck rampage to happen.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How extreme heat is hitting wallets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c99b8888747505710a463cc423f37fa0a7cfa16019cc04236fee0fa4c36aeef2</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-hotter-weather-is-making-us-poorer/a-79268306--10853d8a0a0a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-extreme-heat-is-hitting-wallets/a-79268306?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Heat waves, wildfires and floods have cascading economic impacts, causing incomes to decline and the price of basic goods to rise. The trend will escalate as temperatures continue to increase.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's rights groups, EU call out LGBTQ+ crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f89c90487bdeb8f86198f6319b0af463c2c306e480864af92156d65afa09e357</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021--701b89ffacea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several raids and arrests of LGBTQ+ persons in Turkey have triggered sharp criticism from numerous Turkish organizations — and also from Brussels.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Drivers in Germany fume over soaring fuel prices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d905bfad7129316f26adb572d0b18b565812b61b84faed3ff2620714aec8651e</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/drivers-in-germany-fume-over-soaring-fuel-prices/a-79282456--6a933389e322.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/drivers-in-germany-fume-over-soaring-fuel-prices/a-79282456?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz wants to provide relief to motorists. But exactly how this is to happen remains unclear.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Holocaust survivor on 'very dangerous' AfD Saxony-Anhalt win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:718b7929168913df358aea40807a24145bdc0b1ed8bd7ec0fe52db03771d2d6c</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/holocaust-survivor-on-very-dangerous-afd-saxony-anhalt-win/a-79278429--2441e4b64e9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/holocaust-survivor-on-very-dangerous-afd-saxony-anhalt-win/a-79278429?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Charlotte Knobloch survived the Holocaust by passing as the daughter of non-Jewish farmers. She recently spoke with DW to express her shock following the AfD victory in Saxony-Anhalt's state election.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Why do authoritarian regimes target the LGBTQ+ community?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e7345a14e44d767a0c03343a362d7bc940baf922e43abc2a873f31d7b1c0eb5</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831--8b4048f7a695.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A recent crackdown on the LGBTQ+ community in Turkey is symptomatic of a wider rights regression, according to experts. It's worse under authoritarian regimes, but why is it such a popular policy for these states?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish scientists find first evidence of Diplodocus dinosaur in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86db5eefaaa473614ecd5e7c95091233acfb03c5ea8281a3b2b6a4bdf49535c9</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-scientists-find-first-evidence-of-diplodocus-dinosaur-in-europe/a-79277825--f2d2e7bb0613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-scientists-find-first-evidence-of-diplodocus-dinosaur-in-europe/a-79277825?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paleontologists in Spain say they have found the first evidence of the long-necked Diplodocus genus of dinosaur outside of North America. They found bones at the rich La Tejeria fossil site in Teruel in eastern Spain.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why the era of cheap government debt is over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0de2aced0f2f29db69f0d97432fb05bd23c91d2d6d9d8b3b937abae13ae17f47</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272--435550125c87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US debt has topped $40 trillion. How risky is the country's growing debt burden. And will investors keep funding Washington's deficits?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Netherlands: Suspected sabotage disrupts train services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c95fa3abad2dcc14a762eeabb44f411c790b0f4733b2e144f0a4352706d003f</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600--a0c80c1ea5f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major outage has hit parts of the Dutch railway system after objects were found placed across lines, authorities say. The company responsible for rail infrastructure says it suspects deliberate wrongdoing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why AI researchers warn humanity could face extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e064b7d1d5fc1879b5b346a8a762e8a22fab5b5fa9035768374e6c8fb0bd941</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-ai-researchers-warn-humanity-could-face-extinction/a-79263146--d42b075a07d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-ai-researchers-warn-humanity-could-face-extinction/a-79263146?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Could artificial intelligence pose an existential threat to humanity? Some leading researchers are warning against an unregulated race toward AI superintelligence.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Iran and US: Two countries and the pistachio between them</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b03e988187b9762ccd1470000f27750d4e61877a460767da31c1132df1578878</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-and-us-two-countries-and-the-pistachio-between-them/a-79224310--28756f33fc8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-and-us-two-countries-and-the-pistachio-between-them/a-79224310?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pistachios sold across the United States have a surprising history: California's trees trace their roots to Iran. Now, both regions face the same threat — their farmland is sinking as groundwater disappears.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Europe launches two climate observation satellites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6140ccff371dc127877f5b26d94cefce2237f38b1446bebc6580ee6aba11a325</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705--7858649e62ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Space Agency has put two satellites into orbit to take a closer look at the impact of climate change. One of them will focus particularly on plant life.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks Arctic strategy amid growing power rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:386e5aa3d9e13d4e75f768e22cac6a7a5b3d7c3919fc6501eeddebb87e30bd40</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739--8da58b1eb0cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's aggression, Trump's threats against Greenland and the race for critical raw materials are pushing the Arctic to the top of Europe's agenda.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Russia set for new round of US-mediated talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9904ac08df0e8a5be8aec347e0fc3b270abbd7dc92c700f6ac71d03c2430a2d6</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T18:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147--0cf6c10eaa61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New trilateral talks between Ukraine, Russia and the US could begin in October, according to Kyiv and Moscow. Few expect a breakthrough, but Ukraine is seeking a partial de-escalation to help it get through the winter.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Women's Basketball World Cup: Can Germany harness a boom?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa9082828a05c0842da47e04d8be6ecbe545e5411c82ec0667974c99baf62d7f</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602--77d972e02866.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany thrilled fans at the Women's Basketball World Cup. But even if this sparked a boom in the women's game, the infrastructure simply isn't ready for it.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's richest man Dangote's IPO out of reach in Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cad65b8da9136d5333f1d4238a5c94ba45067de97129c5eb0cf8f5a29dac42ad</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398--03e0d1756308.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dangote seeks $1.6 billion from investors to finance a $14.3 billion expansion and thus double the oil refinery's capacity. The offer could give millions of Nigerians a stake in the company. But who can truly afford it?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The Crusades: How a medieval holy war still shapes politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07e5a92400e25efe8f4dc55b0b2a6b8ffb5e80c459e6ffd091872b40ac6f94d5</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-crusades-how-a-medieval-holy-war-still-shapes-politics/a-79203784--8fa07b173177.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-crusades-how-a-medieval-holy-war-still-shapes-politics/a-79203784?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 1095, the Catholic Church launched the Crusades: wars that left millions dead and whose legacy still shapes political and ideological conflicts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Can Iran replace sea trade with land routes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:035a14e43b672d9e1126a2957672c4d85353dbb0286b31d5f6d23ba02b5a49f9</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179--9748aa6cdc36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran is shifting trade toward northern ports and land routes as its southern shipping faces a US blockade. Analysts say the corridors can keep essential goods moving, but cannot replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Zverev wins US Open in golden year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff6b7cf0c46b72d48ced9079f3afd7284d12b86b66fd6d3882215f527f77f188</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T22:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706--d962ccd6a0c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev has won the US Open for the first time, defeating Ben Shelton in the final. It is Zverev's second Grand Slam win of 2026 after a long wait for his first title, but controversy still hangs over him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why are European banks moving gold out of United States?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38bee224cf6eaeaa8535e3ced72bfe7098fce4a101e6cf57e940d9fc5ffb27fa</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013--320ff1551fa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Netherlands and France have moved their gold out of US vaults. Part of the reason is fears about the reliability of the US, but equally important is the need to keep gold closer to home in the event of a crisis.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Corals as climate archive: Are El Nino events intensifying?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c430979a780de293d13934157af26311f2c5cc2b5b2c606de6de494dbd479569</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-nino-events-intensifying/a-79243425--ac4752671640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-nino-events-intensifying/a-79243425?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Records show that El Nino events have been frequent and often extreme over the past few decades. Is this normal? Or is it the result of climate change? Corals can give us a clear indication.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>India looks to steer BRICS away from anti-Western turn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e580c44fde12d615b40bcc18d822138371b8e7404bdf02cecb0d2fb6791afa4</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234--e9a076e9f28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit 2026 takes place in Delhi this weekend. Unlike last year, Putin and Xi are expected to attend. Can India keep the expanded bloc united?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>The 'end of an era' as Goethe-Institut in Russia closes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cda291875f6c2a46ade2bbe8b4c383d86d6ade670f648ba50137a0876ce33fe</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321--189393464061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Goethe-Institut was one of the last German institutions still operating in Russia. However, following Moscow's decision to close its offices, all employees will have to stop working by September 13.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Celine Dion became a pop culture icon across generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:964cb4c7cca8253a4b57e0d0ab74c882687519bc92f7f41dc6e4de399599a308</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-celine-dion-became-a-pop-culture-icon-across-generations/a-79213779--40db204d1ea8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-celine-dion-became-a-pop-culture-icon-across-generations/a-79213779?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the global star kicks off her anticipated Paris residency, here's how Celine Dion managed to gain younger followers while keeping her loyal older fans.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Belarusians still find hope in a silenced country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe04df071ec273eb7b43e99b0bec812bda101c8dd2056084942713c406ed641a</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285--d234556fa838.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The documentary "Letters from the Silenced Country" depicts the ongoing repression under the authoritarian regime. Director Andrei Kutsila talked to DW ahead of the film's Venice premiere.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Why we're still looking 